WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:19.810
The ancient fortress stood on a craggy, windswept ridge on the western slope of Mount Mystery.

2
00:00:19.811 --> 00:00:26.147
Miles of dense, shadowy forest guarded by fearsome creatures separated it from the rest of Magica.

3
00:00:26.148 --> 00:00:29.319
Most people had forgotten the fortress was even there.

4
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:37.719
But to those who remembered, it was a reminder of the Old Times, when Magica was not the peaceful place it was now.

5
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:44.173
A gaunt man with glittering amber eyes stood at a high window staring down at the forest.

6
00:00:44.174 --> 00:00:48.326
He heard a grunt and turned to see that a troll had entered.

7
00:00:48.327 --> 00:00:52.243
"What is it?" the man demanded.

8
00:00:52.244 --> 00:01:01.357
The troll grunted again. A puff of magic energy rose above him, showing a rough image of ugly troll teeth tearing into food.

9
00:01:01.358 --> 00:01:04.807
Hungry. The trolls were hungry.

10
00:01:04.808 --> 00:01:08.341
"You'll have to wait a little longer," the man said.

11
00:01:08.342 --> 00:01:11.965
"But soon you'll have all the food you want."

12
00:01:11.966 --> 00:01:15.313
He stepped over to the contraption in the center of the room.

13
00:01:15.314 --> 00:01:17.647
He'd finished building it moments ago.

14
00:01:17.648 --> 00:01:26.715
It was a mishmash of many things: dragon bones and scales, leather-bound books, stones gathered from the Cave of the Unknown, and more.

15
00:01:26.716 --> 00:01:31.850
At the very top of the pile was an ancient human skull bleached white by time.

16
00:01:31.851 --> 00:01:36.627
The man rubbed his hands together and placed them over the skull's eye sockets.

17
00:01:36.628 --> 00:01:43.318
The machine shuddered to life and belched out an image: a map of all of Magica.

18
00:01:43.319 --> 00:01:48.700
Tiny red dots glowed here and there. Hundreds of them! The man smiled.

19
00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:57.593
The Secret Eye worked, just as the ancient writings had predicted. This would make things much easier.

20
00:01:57.594 --> 00:02:03.861
It was time to go and take what was rightfully his.

21
00:02:03.862 --> 00:02:09.865
"Zann, you're next. Zann. Zann! ZANN!"

22
00:02:09.866 --> 00:02:12.424
Zann blinked and looked at the teacher.

23
00:02:12.425 --> 00:02:16.552
"Sorry, Professor Liblow," he said. "Could you repeat that?"

24
00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:19.091
Several of Zann's classmates laughed.

25
00:02:19.092 --> 00:02:24.861
"It's your turn to perform today's exercise," Professor Liblow said patiently.

26
00:02:24.862 --> 00:02:29.461
"Please move your assigned objects according to my instructions."

27
00:02:29.462 --> 00:02:34.440
"Oh. Okay." Zann stood up. Everyone was watching him.

28
00:02:34.441 --> 00:02:39.791
He had no idea what instructions the teacher had given or what his assigned objects were.

29
00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.928
He'd been too busy daydreaming.

30
00:02:41.929 --> 00:02:44.411
He looked at the table at the front of the room.

31
00:02:44.412 --> 00:02:49.791
All sorts of things were sitting there—fruit, rocks, shoes, and more.

32
00:02:49.792 --> 00:02:52.172
Which items was he supposed to move?

33
00:02:52.173 --> 00:02:56.804
"Books," a voice hissed behind him, too softly for the teacher to hear.

34
00:02:56.805 --> 00:02:59.857
"You're supposed to stack them by size."

35
00:02:59.858 --> 00:03:04.889
It was Perda, his next-door neighbor and friend. He shot her a grateful look.

36
00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:09.670
Then he glanced at the books. Transporting stuff was easy.

37
00:03:09.671 --> 00:03:16.296
But it wasn't easy to do it with the control and precision that the teacher wanted. Especially for someone like Zann.

38
00:03:16.297 --> 00:03:24.102
He was good at bigger magic, like zapping himself to a new place or creating clothing or food out of nothing.

39
00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:27.812
This smaller, more detailed type of magic was not easy.

40
00:03:27.813 --> 00:03:32.456
It required a quiet mind, and Zann's mind was rarely quiet.

41
00:03:32.457 --> 00:03:35.178
He rubbed his thumb against his other fingers.

42
00:03:35.179 --> 00:03:38.951
There was a crackling sound as sparks began to jump from his hand.

43
00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:45.174
Zann pointed at the largest book, and everything on the table flew into the air and exploded.

44
00:03:45.175 --> 00:03:49.062
The other students giggled, and Zann smiled sheepishly.

45
00:03:49.063 --> 00:03:52.357
"Oops," he said. "Sorry about that."

46
00:03:52.358 --> 00:03:55.140
Professor Liblow rubbed his hands together.

47
00:03:55.141 --> 00:04:03.921
"Restore!" he said. The items reappeared. "Try again, please, Zann. And try to focus this time.

48
00:04:03.922 --> 00:04:10.308
We don't want you accidentally transporting the entire school to the peak of Mount Mystery."

49
00:04:10.309 --> 00:04:13.403
That made everyone laugh, including Zann.

50
00:04:13.404 --> 00:04:17.578
Then he tried again. This time he did his best to focus.

51
00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:20.107
"Come to me," he murmured.

52
00:04:20.108 --> 00:04:22.756
Now only the largest book rose.

53
00:04:22.757 --> 00:04:26.148
It flew through the air and landed gently on his desk.

54
00:04:26.149 --> 00:04:29.371
One by one, he brought the other books to him.

55
00:04:29.372 --> 00:04:35.737
Finally a slim volume titled Dragon Taming Tips landed neatly atop the pile.

56
00:04:35.738 --> 00:04:39.292
Most of the class clapped. Zann gave a playful bow.

57
00:04:39.293 --> 00:04:45.127
"Pretty slow," a boy said loudly. "And you had to use a focusing phrase.

58
00:04:45.128 --> 00:04:49.054
I thought Reds were supposed to be better at magic than the rest of us."

59
00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:56.040
"Enough, Jev," the teacher said sternly. "If you think you can do better, you may go next."

60
00:04:56.041 --> 00:05:01.408
Zann sat down. "Thanks for saving me," he whispered to his friend.

61
00:05:01.409 --> 00:05:07.354
Perda leaned forward. "No problem. But you really should pay attention," she whispered.

62
00:05:07.355 --> 00:05:11.208
"Even Reds can't just fake their way through every class they don't like."

63
00:05:11.209 --> 00:05:16.262
Zann didn't answer. Physical Objects was one of his least favorite classes.

64
00:05:16.263 --> 00:05:20.502
It was boring—even more boring than Food and Drink Creation.

65
00:05:20.503 --> 00:05:24.149
When would he ever need to move things around like that, anyway?

66
00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:28.891
He wasn't planning on becoming a physical builder or anything of the sort. No way.

67
00:05:28.892 --> 00:05:31.800
He was going to be an explorer like his parents.

68
00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:36.376
That's why he spent most of his time in school daydreaming about exciting adventures.

69
00:05:36.377 --> 00:05:41.474
"I'm finished!" Jev announced as he lined up one last shoe on his desk.

70
00:05:41.475 --> 00:05:45.711
He shot Zann a smug look. "Much faster than the Red."

71
00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:49.934
Zann frowned. Jev always had to make him look bad.

72
00:05:49.935 --> 00:05:53.708
Just then a pretty girl named Gliss pointed to the door.

73
00:05:53.709 --> 00:05:57.320
Gliss was the only other Red in the class besides Zann.

74
00:05:57.321 --> 00:05:59.704
"An echo crow!" she cried.

75
00:05:59.705 --> 00:06:05.723
A large, purple-feathered crow flapped into the room.

76
00:06:05.724 --> 00:06:11.189
"Message! Message!" it squawked. "Urgent message from the king and queen!"

77
00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:15.180
Several kids gasped, and Zann sat up straight in his chair.

78
00:06:15.181 --> 00:06:22.146
He couldn't remember anyone from Magica's capital, First City, sending a message to boring old Swamp Bottom before.

79
00:06:22.147 --> 00:06:24.387
Especially not the king and queen!

80
00:06:24.388 --> 00:06:30.437
"Hush," Professor Liblow told the class. Then he nodded to the crow. "Go on, please."

81
00:06:30.438 --> 00:06:41.502
"Urgent! Danger!" the crow squawked. "Danger for all Reds!"
